{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: test_principal_member (Layer-2, app-owned; TEST fixture).
  Permits a tool only when the calling PRINCIPAL (the bearer's user, not the browser
  session) holds mcp.tokens.manage — i.e. an approved member (role mcp_user or
  mcp_operator). Unlike the shipped `members_can_write` (which allows any authenticated
  caller), this distinguishes an approved member from a bare token holder, so the
  coverage suite can prove per-principal tool visibility and authz-deny.
  Fail-closed: no profile or no permission → deny.
  Contract: return { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent, arguments, tool,
  delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function allow = 'modules/mcp/queries/principal/can', principal: principal, do: 'mcp.tokens.manage'
  assign r = {}
  assign r['allow'] = allow
  if allow
    assign r['reason'] = 'member'
  else
    assign r['reason'] = 'not_member'
  endif
  return r
%}
